On Wednesday, January 11, 2017 at 2:19:36 AM UTC-5, Tadaishi Yatabe wrote:
> Thanks a lot for the help Ben. I managed to run the code you provided with my data and it looks good. Although, as you say, the constraints on lambda seem off, as with the current one lambda is a positive number (indicating overdispersion, when in fact variance in this data is less than half of the mean). I'm trying to define a function as you said...but no success yet.

You just need to call a user-defined function that returns the lower bound, like

functions {
  real lb(matrix X, vector beta) {
    real max_mu = max(exp(X * beta));
    if (max_mu <= 2) return max_mu / (max_mu - 4);
    return -1;
  }
}

Then, in the parameters block

parameters {
  vector[K] beta;
  real<lower=lb(X, beta), upper = 1> lambda;
}

Ben

