On Tue, Jan 24, 2017 at 9:41 PM, Andrew Gelman <gel...@stat.columbia.edu> wrote:

> I agree that the fake-data check is not perfect, but it's something.  I was pushing back against Jonah's statement, "in order to trust it you'll have to run NUTS anyway, in which case you might as well just use NUTS."  That's fine, but suppose you have a problem where Nuts is too slow to run.  Then you have to do some approx.  ADVI is one choice.

Yeah my comment doesn't really apply in the case of a problem that is still too time consuming for running NUTS to be feasible.

On another note, one thing that does sometimes help when using advi is Ben's trick of applying a scaled QR decomposition to the X matrix in a regression model.

