Hi Daniel (and others)

Briefly put, I am working on a model to estimate latent positions of political actors from survey data, and I am using MC simulations to compare its performance to existing models, showing where the latter fall short. I would be happy to share the code, data, and paper, and would be very grateful for any comments and advice. I don’t want to make it public before it (hopefully) gets published (which would still be far into the future), but I could e-mail it those interested (unless you have a better suggestion for sharing privately). I should probably spend a few days cleaning up the code and the paper first though.

I hope the paper will illustrate that ADVI can be useful for simulations — although, in line with Michael’s point, I will only use ADVI to get approximate point estimates, and use NUTS when I need to sample the full posteriors. (For me the choice depends on whether I want to fit the model a few thousand times, and whether I can make do with the point estimates — I hope to be able to justify using ADVI for these situations.)

Best,
Joergen

